From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Fri, 19 Jun 2026 18:14:21 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02901/11362] [outer-loop] fix two submission-breaking
 make_carnot_agent adapter bugs vs live framework
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Pre-submission diff of make_carnot_agent against the real ARC-AGI-3-Agents
Agent base (agents/agent.py) surfaced two bugs that NO offline test caught —
both offline validators drive policy.next_move() directly and never exercise
the adapter's choose_action, which is what the live harness calls:

1. CRITICAL: choose_action returned act.set_data(data), but GameAction.set_data()
   returns the inner ComplexAction, NOT the enum. do_action_request reads
   action.action_data off the return, so a ComplexAction crashes EVERY click
   action (AttributeError: 'ComplexAction' has no attribute 'action_data').
   Verified against the real arcengine.GameAction. Fix: mutate in place, return
   the enum, carry game_id (required ComplexAction field, as Playback does).

2. Agent.MAX_ACTIONS default is 80 — too low even for our deepest banked replay
   (lp85 -> L5). Override to 400 so multi-level replays + held-out-game explore
   have room; the eval's <=12h wall-clock is the real bound.

Adds tests/python/test_arc_competition_agent_adapter.py (4 tests, pass) pinning
both fixes via the real GameAction enum + the framework's exact consumption.

